                <pb facs="0739" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg589"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul-General Kent to Chargé Brown.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consular Service</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 458.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I inclose you a copy of a letter
                    received from Mr. Reed, American consular agent at Livingston, in reference to a
                    condition of affairs existing within his jurisdiction, which he fears may become
                    applicable to American citizens.</p>
                <p>I am unable to advise him myself, and refer the matter to you and will transmit
                    to him your opinion upon the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. P. Kent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
